@startuml sequence_diagram_switch_active_layout
autonumber
skinparam shadowing true
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

title Sequence Diagram - VIS02 Switching the Active Kitchen Configuration (AC 4)

actor Manager as "LaPrizza Manager"
participant Page as "Kitchen configurations page\n(WEB06)"
participant BE as "Back-End API\n(WEB06)"
participant Viewer as "KitchenViewer\n(VIS01)"
participant Engine as "ViewerEngine\n(VIS01)"
participant Old as "KitchenLayoutModule\n(compact)"
participant New as "KitchenLayoutModule\n(extended)"
participant Assets as "LoadedAssets\n(VIS01)"

note over Manager, Assets
    Precondition: KCF-00001 "Compact kitchen" (12 x 8 x 3.2 m, line on the NORTH wall) is ACTIVE and shown
    by the viewer (state "ready", sequence_diagram_build_kitchen_layout).
    The viewer never keeps a previous layout: every load rebuilds the scene from the configuration that is
    ACTIVE at that moment (VIS01 BR 4 / BR 8). A module instance is never reused between loads.
end note

== 1. Activation in WEB06 (usWEB06 SD 3) ==

Manager -> Page : activates KCF-00002 "Extended assembly line"\n(16 x 10 x 3.5 m, line on the EAST wall) and confirms
activate Page
Page -> BE : POST /kitchen-configurations/KCF-00002/activation
activate BE
BE --> Page : 200 { activeConfiguration: { id: "KCF-00002", name, status: "ACTIVE",\nversion, elementCount, updatedAt, activatedAt },\npreviousActiveConfigurationId: "KCF-00001" }
deactivate BE
Page --> Manager : "Extended assembly line is now the active configuration"\n+ "Open / reload the kitchen viewer"
deactivate Page

== 2. Reload of the viewer (usVIS01 SD 2) ==

Manager -> Viewer : "Open / reload the kitchen viewer" (fresh mount)\nor "Reload" inside the viewer
activate Viewer
Viewer -> Engine : dispose()  (previous attempt, BEFORE the new one)
activate Engine
Engine -> Engine : stop the render loop
Engine -> Old : dispose()  (modules in reverse order)
activate Old
Old -> Old : scene.remove("layout:root")\nshapes.dispose() - procedural geometries, once\nroom geometries dispose()\nmaterials.dispose() - materials created for this build\nclones: skeleton.dispose() if skinned; disposed = true
note right of Old : geometries / materials / textures of the\nimported files are NOT touched (BR 10)
Old --> Engine : done
deactivate Old
Engine -> Assets : dispose()  (imported files of the compact kitchen, once)
Engine -> Engine : renderer.dispose(); forceContextLoss()
deactivate Engine
Viewer -> Viewer : new attempt with a fresh canvas (VIS01 D17)

Viewer -> BE : GET /kitchen-configurations/active (through kitchenViewerApi, VIS01)
activate BE
BE --> Viewer : 200 KCF-00002 version 4 + assets of the extended kitchen
deactivate BE

alt A) Preload or engine failure (e.g. a model file of KCF-00002 unavailable)
    Viewer --> Manager : state "error" (asset-unavailable + asset id) or "failed" + [Retry]
    note right of Viewer : interaction ends: the compact kitchen is NOT\nshown again - only the active one can be shown
else B) Every asset of KCF-00002 preloaded
    Viewer -> Engine : create(...) ; load(KCF-00002, newLoadedAssets, factories)
    activate Engine
    Engine -> New : build(SceneContext of KCF-00002)
    activate New
    New -> New : room 16 x 10 x 3.5 m;\none object per EQUIPMENT element of KCF-00002 (14)\nwith its own position / rotation / scale
    New --> Engine : "layout:root" added to the scene
    deactivate New
    Engine -> Engine : VIS03 builds the 9 assembly-line elements on the EAST wall;\nVIS05-VIS06 modules; VIS07 computes the initial pose\nfor the 16 x 10 x 3.5 m room (single owner of the camera)
    Viewer -> Engine : start()
    deactivate Engine
    Viewer --> Manager : state "ready": extended kitchen only; no object\nof the compact kitchen remains (ids, room size)
end
deactivate Viewer

@enduml